{"id": "EUVD-2026-85945", "enisaUuid": "fd868d96-537e-37cf-9eb3-4a02a2a5e528", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmm/page_owner: use memcg_data snapshot to avoid TOCTOU in print_page_owner_memcg()\n\nprint_page_owner_memcg() reads page->memcg_data via READ_ONCE() at the\nstart to guard against tail pages and NULL data.  However, it later\nre-reads page->memcg_data locklessly in two places:\n\n1: page_memcg_check(page)\n\n2: PageMemcgKmem(page) (via folio_memcg_kmem(), which includes\n   VM_BUG_ON assertions for tail pages and MEMCG_DATA_OBJEXTS)\n\nIf the page is concurrently freed and reallocated as a THP tail page or\nslab page between these calls, the VM_BUG_ON assertions can trigger on\nCONFIG_DEBUG_VM=y builds, crashing the kernel.\n\nFix both TOCTOU issues by using the memcg_data snapshot throughout.", "datePublished": "2026-09-24T15:10:38", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:52:21", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e7c1923c5f30a6953f0540e3171d882ec17b05d3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a4c940ab3f794f221a338c9431ad1ce0d73a2bea", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/46761406e14381dc35f498c247a87565b87ea2ef", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/90f095b816e25c6a9e4446d299bac5007fdcb3df"], "aliases": ["GHSA-rrh5-8w69-2q6j", "CVE-2026-93216"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1244ae13-8caf-31b7-b23d-579d7dfc80b4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "245e9df3-1c62-32ac-a6cd-37b9ae449d0d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "fcf8935832b86d3437f00e732c6d0d4d2819d6a9 <90f095b816e25c6a9e4446d299bac5007fdcb3df"}, {"id": "4a9c6166-2704-396c-87f7-f6364a4a61ed", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "fcf8935832b86d3437f00e732c6d0d4d2819d6a9 <e7c1923c5f30a6953f0540e3171d882ec17b05d3"}, {"id": "61dbefe9-b646-3899-a70e-8a8b6a55f3bf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.18"}, {"id": "68273158-6e28-3b1c-b251-3a19fc5f2b0e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "fcf8935832b86d3437f00e732c6d0d4d2819d6a9 <46761406e14381dc35f498c247a87565b87ea2ef"}, {"id": "ad87aa5d-7587-31d0-bb05-455c08d2df73", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.4"}, {"id": "ae794e11-9e34-3e36-b037-9bc7fec73e85", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "bb3fa626-326e-3aff-b888-7c8f24c763c0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "c761a160-82a8-3b6f-ba3c-833585d5ff18", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "fcf8935832b86d3437f00e732c6d0d4d2819d6a9 <a4c940ab3f794f221a338c9431ad1ce0d73a2bea"}, {"id": "df7a0f91-98e8-3ff5-9c49-ad0ed80bab23", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "0fb697de-5011-3d2a-b2c6-dfb9c484c0c1", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}